From d797f618b37f82a9c1a399211d985ca00ba41ab2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:27:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Firewall log: NFLOG collector rflogd, a fallback log path,
 day files on the store

- Every firewall log rule takes its target from shared/reaper_fwlog.h: NFLOG to the new collector
  rflogd while it runs (groups 40 stock chains, 41 Warden, 42 the anti-botnet chains, 43 the rules
  engine), under a flood ceiling of 10000 lines a second per rule (burst 10000, the most the limit
  match takes); else a limited LOG at level 5, 10 a second. The choice is made each time a rule
  set is written or a Warden / rules-engine script runs, so a collector that stops or comes back
  needs no regeneration. It replaces the 2026-11-07 rate limit alone.
- rflogd (rflogd/) reads the four groups, keeps a ring of the newest lines for the pages, counts
  lines, losses and what the ceiling held back (stats.json), forwards to the remote log server
  when one is set, and writes one file a day under <store>/fwlog/ on a USB long-term store (up to
  30 days or 256 MB, the oldest day removed first). Its timers run on the monotonic clock; a day
  file is never dated before the image was built.
- rc/reaper_fwlog.c: rflog_sync starts or refreshes rflogd and writes the log path; the watchdog
  checks it every 2 s and swaps the path both ways. firewall.c routes the stock chains, the
  anti-botnet chains' LOG lines (from their rule text, IPv4 and IPv6) and the rules engine through
  it; rwarden.c and reaper_fw.c their own.
- httpd/web.c: the collector's counters and ring for the pages, its day files in the store's
  dataset list and sizes. The Firewall page shows the collector state (RFW_413 / RFW_414); the
  System Log has a Firewall view (RLOG_102 / RLOG_103); the Storage page a Firewall log row, USB
  only (RDST_113..115). New installs list fwlog among the durable datasets (shared/defaults.c);
  existing lists are not touched.
Also in these files: web.c refuses a WireGuard .conf without its keys and reports whether
/jffs/scripts/ddns-start exists (the WireGuard and DDNS commits), and counts a failed login
against its source (the login commit); services.c acts on a pending Let's Encrypt request on the
Custom DDNS path too, and no longer starts fsmd; watchdog.c skips a missing dnsqd (the
unused-programs commit); rc.h raises the AiMesh exemption table from 64 to 256 entries (16
tri-band nodes had filled it) and declares the WireGuard DNS-rule purge; Reaper_Firewall.asp gives
every add row of Objects / Zones / Egress / Forwards its own message line (an Address groups Add
had reported on the hidden Rules tab, so it looked like nothing happened) and names a group member
that is not an address object (RFW_412), and shows a long-term store on a volume without
permissions as one note.

